 **Measured Performance**
-The method is part of the Full SNS model. In ablation studies (Table 4 in [S1, unofficial]), the Full SNS (including k-decomposition and Alternating Optimization) generally outperforms ablated versions. For example, on the "Playroom Blending Deep" scene, the Full SNS achieved a PSNR of 30.7130, compared to 30.6745 for a version without the full combination. On average across datasets, the Full SNS achieved a PSNR of 30.3034, compared to 30.2969 for a baseline without the full combination [S1, unofficial].
